WEBVTT

00:00:00.311 --> 00:00:02.211
Dominoes Starter Level.

00:00:02.231 --> 00:00:04.772
A Pretty Face by John

00:00:04.792 --> 00:00:05.222
Escott.

00:00:05.282 --> 00:00:06.832
Read by Jennifer J.

00:00:06.872 --> 00:00:07.012
Myers.

00:00:07.052 --> 00:00:10.113
Copyright Oxford University Press 2003.

00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:10.653
Chapter 1.

00:00:10.713 --> 00:00:21.706
Zoe Is Angry

00:00:21.765 --> 00:00:34.800
Zoe is 17 years old.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:41.365
She works in a bookstore in the little town of Newport.

00:00:41.425 --> 00:00:47.259
Zoe likes books, and she likes her work.

00:00:47.319 --> 00:00:55.541
But after work, she likes to act in plays with the Newport Players.

00:00:55.601 --> 00:01:05.570
The Newport Players do six plays every year and Zoe is in most of them.

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:12.442
Some plays are exciting and some plays are famous.

00:01:12.502 --> 00:01:22.179
This week the play is Romeo and Juliet by William Shakespeare.

00:01:22.239 --> 00:01:28.556
A lot of people are coming to see it, Zoe thinks.

00:01:28.616 --> 00:01:32.107
I must act well.

00:01:32.166 --> 00:01:37.138
Mike is 18 years old.

00:01:37.198 --> 00:01:44.820
He is a student at Newport College and he likes writing.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:53.525
One day, he wants to write plays for the theatre and for television.

00:01:53.585 --> 00:02:00.902
One day, I want to be famous, he thinks.

00:02:00.962 --> 00:02:04.986
Newport has a newspaper.

00:02:05.045 --> 00:02:09.899
The Newport Weekly News is its name.

00:02:09.958 --> 00:02:14.913
And Mike's Aunt Peggy is the editor.

00:02:14.972 --> 00:02:19.962
One morning, she phones Mike.

00:02:20.022 --> 00:02:29.966
Do you want to write a review of Romeo and Juliet for the newspaper, Mike?"

00:02:30.026 --> 00:02:32.528
She asks him.

00:02:32.588 --> 00:02:40.944
The Newport Players are doing the play tonight at the Little Theatre.

00:02:41.004 --> 00:02:45.017
Yes, please, Aunt Peggy.

00:02:45.077 --> 00:02:49.996
Mike says, thanks for asking me.

00:02:50.056 --> 00:02:58.647
That evening he goes to Newport's Little Theatre to see the play.

00:02:58.707 --> 00:03:05.082
Mike goes into the theatre and sits at the front.

00:03:05.142 --> 00:03:14.328
He gets out his notebook and pen ready to write notes for his review.

00:03:14.388 --> 00:03:27.608
There are a lot of people in the audience. Five minutes later, the play begins.

00:03:27.628 --> 00:03:31.770
Zoe acts the part of Juliet's mother.

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:37.954
She knows all her words and speaks them well.

00:03:38.014 --> 00:03:41.906
Mike is watching her.

00:03:41.966 --> 00:03:45.180
She's very pretty.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:49.754
And she's doing her best, he thinks.

00:03:49.814 --> 00:03:56.080
But it's not easy to act the part of an older woman.

00:03:56.140 --> 00:04:04.254
She's only 16 or 17 years old, and we all know it.

00:04:04.314 --> 00:04:09.090
He begins to write in his notebook.

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:17.557
Two hours later, the play ends and the audience leaves the theatre.

00:04:17.617 --> 00:04:23.960
Mike goes home and writes his review for the newspaper.

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:28.402
He doesn't feel very happy.

00:04:28.462 --> 00:04:40.828
It was a good play, but what can I say about the girl acting a part of Juliet's mother, he thinks.

00:04:40.888 --> 00:04:48.372
I want to be kind, but I must be honest too.

00:04:48.432 --> 00:04:59.204
At the bookstore on Friday, Zoe reads Mike's review of the play in the Newport Weekly News.

00:04:59.264 --> 00:05:05.075
And Zoe Baker acts the part of Juliet's mother.

00:05:05.135 --> 00:05:11.082
She has a pretty face, and she speaks her words well.

00:05:11.142 --> 00:05:19.730
But she is a young girl in an older woman's costume, and we all know it.

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:24.742
She can never make me believe differently.

00:05:24.802 --> 00:05:28.232
Zoe is angry.

00:05:28.292 --> 00:05:32.654
She looks at the name under the review.

00:05:32.714 --> 00:05:36.058
Mike Morrison.

00:05:36.118 --> 00:05:40.584
Who is this Mike Morrison?

00:05:40.643 --> 00:05:42.374
She thinks.

00:05:42.434 --> 00:05:47.106
What does he know about acting?

00:05:47.166 --> 00:05:59.032
Chapter 2 Zoe has an idea.

00:05:59.092 --> 00:06:16.908
On Tuesday evening the next week, Zoe and her friend Annie are drinking coffee in the Newport Café.

00:06:16.968 --> 00:06:29.240
Annie is a student at Newport College and sometimes in the evenings she and Zoe meet at the cafe.

00:06:29.299 --> 00:06:37.739
Suddenly, Zoe sees a boy sitting at a table across the room.

00:06:37.798 --> 00:06:40.599
Who's that boy?

00:06:40.659 --> 00:06:43.200
She asks Annie.

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:45.390
Annie laughs.

00:06:45.450 --> 00:06:47.310
Do you like him?

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:51.131
He has a nice face, she says.

00:06:51.191 --> 00:06:53.272
His name's Mike.

00:06:53.332 --> 00:06:57.189
I often see him at the college.

00:06:57.248 --> 00:07:02.907
Mike, Zoe says, Mike who?

00:07:02.967 --> 00:07:07.278
Mike Morrison, Annie says.

00:07:07.338 --> 00:07:10.940
That's Mike Morrison?

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:15.752
Zoe says, she is furious.

00:07:15.811 --> 00:07:18.442
Yes, why?

00:07:18.502 --> 00:07:20.499
Annie asks.

00:07:20.559 --> 00:07:28.318
He writes reviews for the Newport Weekly News, Zoe says.

00:07:28.378 --> 00:07:32.090
That's right, Annie says.

00:07:32.150 --> 00:07:34.550
His aunt is the editor.

00:07:34.570 --> 00:07:42.294
Oh, she stops suddenly and looks at Zoe.

00:07:42.354 --> 00:07:46.254
The review of Romeo and Juliet.

00:07:46.314 --> 00:07:49.335
Right, Zoe says.

00:07:49.395 --> 00:07:51.737
Do you remember it?

00:07:51.797 --> 00:07:56.830
Zoe Baker acts the part of Juliet's mother.

00:07:56.890 --> 00:08:03.016
She has a pretty face, and she speaks her words well.

00:08:03.076 --> 00:08:12.833
But she is a young girl in an older woman's costume, and we all know it.

00:08:12.892 --> 00:08:17.266
Nice face or no nice face.

00:08:17.326 --> 00:08:19.688
I hate him.

00:08:19.748 --> 00:08:22.150
Annie laughs.

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:26.864
Okay, go and tell him, she says.

00:08:26.924 --> 00:08:32.238
Go and say, I hate you, Mike Morrison.

00:08:32.298 --> 00:08:36.921
You write stupid reviews for the newspaper.

00:08:36.981 --> 00:08:39.032
Go on.

00:08:39.092 --> 00:08:43.113
But Zoe isn't laughing.

00:08:43.172 --> 00:08:52.726
Yes, all right, she says furiously, and she begins to get up from her chair.

00:08:52.786 --> 00:08:56.908
Then she stops suddenly.

00:08:56.968 --> 00:08:58.820
What's wrong?

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:00.721
Annie asks.

00:09:00.781 --> 00:09:03.002
Are you afraid?

00:09:03.062 --> 00:09:06.545
No, Zoe says.

00:09:06.605 --> 00:09:10.170
I have a better idea.

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:15.635
Does he come into this cafe often?

00:09:15.695 --> 00:09:22.850
Every Tuesday and Thursday evening, I think, Annie says.

00:09:22.911 --> 00:09:31.336
He has a writing class at the college, and he comes here after it finishes.

00:09:31.396 --> 00:09:35.928
Zoe thinks for a minute or two.

00:09:35.988 --> 00:09:42.458
That's very interesting, she says at last.

00:09:42.518 --> 00:09:44.038
Is it?

00:09:44.098 --> 00:09:45.970
Annie says.

00:09:46.030 --> 00:09:52.372
She looks across at Mike Morrison, then at Zoe.

00:09:52.432 --> 00:09:55.683
Why is it interesting?

00:09:55.743 --> 00:09:59.251
What are you thinking of doing?

00:09:59.311 --> 00:10:04.311
Tell me, am I a good actress?"

00:10:04.371 --> 00:10:06.162
Zoe asks.

00:10:06.222 --> 00:10:09.695
Yes, you are, Annie says.

00:10:09.755 --> 00:10:14.388
But, okay, Zoe says.

00:10:14.448 --> 00:10:24.055
I'm a good actress, and I want to prove it to Mr. Mike Nice-Face Morrison.

00:10:24.116 --> 00:10:29.570
How do you want to do that, Annie asks?

00:10:29.630 --> 00:10:36.134
Zoe smiles and begins to tell Annie about her idea.

00:10:36.154 --> 00:11:01.965
Chapter 3: A Difficult Interview. On Thursday, Mike comes to the Newport Café after his writing class.

00:11:02.025 --> 00:11:09.698
He asks for a cup of coffee, then starts to read one of his books.

00:11:09.758 --> 00:11:16.256
Some minutes later, a woman comes into the cafe.

00:11:16.316 --> 00:11:21.608
She is carrying a magazine under her arm.

00:11:21.668 --> 00:11:27.402
At first, Mike does not see the woman.

00:11:27.462 --> 00:11:32.754
Then she comes across to his table.

00:11:32.814 --> 00:11:36.776
Hello, she says.

00:11:36.836 --> 00:11:40.666
Are you Mike Morrison?

00:11:40.726 --> 00:11:43.708
Mike is surprised.

00:11:43.768 --> 00:11:46.300
Yes, he says.

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:48.262
That's me.

00:11:48.322 --> 00:11:51.285
The woman smiles.

00:11:51.345 --> 00:11:55.159
Can I sit at this table?

00:11:55.219 --> 00:11:57.071
She asks.

00:11:57.131 --> 00:11:59.574
Yes, of course.

00:11:59.634 --> 00:12:01.924
Mike says.

00:12:01.983 --> 00:12:08.294
My name is Kate Lawson," the woman says.

00:12:08.354 --> 00:12:12.395
I'm the editor of Yes Magazine.

00:12:12.455 --> 00:12:14.936
Do you know it?

00:12:14.996 --> 00:12:22.238
She sits down and puts the magazine on the table in front of Mike.

00:12:22.298 --> 00:12:26.500
Yes, I know it, Mike says.

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:30.816
It's a magazine about famous people.

00:12:30.876 --> 00:12:35.134
That's right, Kate says.

00:12:35.194 --> 00:12:38.968
Do you want to write something for it?

00:12:39.028 --> 00:12:42.442
Can you do an interview for me?

00:12:42.462 --> 00:12:48.989
An interview, Mike says, surprised.

00:12:49.049 --> 00:12:52.825
Why are you asking me?

00:12:52.885 --> 00:13:01.630
You sometimes write theatre reviews for the Newport Weekly News, she says.

00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:03.851
Is that right?

00:13:03.911 --> 00:13:08.242
Yes, I do, he says.

00:13:08.302 --> 00:13:18.776
I want to write plays one day and, well, do this interview for my magazine then, she says.

00:13:18.836 --> 00:13:22.106
It's with a famous playwright.

00:13:22.166 --> 00:13:25.516
He lives in Newport.

00:13:25.576 --> 00:13:32.578
Todd Marin is the only famous playwright in Newport, Mike says.

00:13:32.638 --> 00:13:44.892
He lives quietly and doesn't go out very often, and he's famous for not talking to reporters from gossip magazines.

00:13:44.952 --> 00:13:48.483
He throws them out of his house.

00:13:48.543 --> 00:13:50.884
Kate laughs.

00:13:50.945 --> 00:13:53.156
Are you afraid?

00:13:53.216 --> 00:13:54.678
She says.

00:13:54.738 --> 00:14:00.924
Good reporters aren't afraid to do difficult interviews.

00:14:00.984 --> 00:14:05.048
You want to write plays, don't you?

00:14:05.108 --> 00:14:12.185
Well, perhaps he can tell you something about playwriting.

00:14:12.245 --> 00:14:17.094
Mike thinks, “She’s right.

00:14:17.154 --> 00:14:22.420
Perhaps I can learn something from Todd Marin.

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:28.254
Okay, he says, when can I do it?

00:14:28.314 --> 00:14:32.484
Tomorrow morning, Kate says.

00:14:32.544 --> 00:14:38.878
You must tell Marin, this interview is for Yes Magazine.

00:14:38.938 --> 00:14:44.641
But tell him after you get into the house, okay?

00:14:44.701 --> 00:14:48.703
Okay, Mike says.

00:14:48.763 --> 00:14:53.315
End of side one.

00:14:53.375 --> 00:15:00.674
Side two.

00:15:00.734 --> 00:15:06.912
Chapter 4.

00:15:06.972 --> 00:15:21.428
Todd Marin's House. Later that evening, Zoe is speaking to Annie on the phone.

00:15:21.488 --> 00:15:29.690
So I say to him, I'm the editor of Yes Magazine.

00:15:29.750 --> 00:15:33.843
And can you interview Todd Marin?

00:15:33.903 --> 00:15:36.436
Zoe tells Annie.

00:15:36.496 --> 00:15:46.324
Todd Marin, Annie says, but he throws gossip magazine reporters out of his house.

00:15:46.384 --> 00:15:48.294
I know.

00:15:48.354 --> 00:16:02.096
Zoe says laughing, and I want to stand outside his house and watch Todd Marin throw Mike Morrison out.

00:16:02.156 --> 00:16:08.987
The next morning Mike goes to Todd Marin's house.

00:16:09.047 --> 00:16:18.574
It is a big house and there are lots of bushes and tall trees in front of it.

00:16:18.634 --> 00:16:29.030
I don't like Yes Magazine very much, but this is an important interview, Mike thinks.

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:35.638
And perhaps I can talk to Todd Marin about my play.

00:16:35.698 --> 00:16:40.584
Mike is writing a play for television.

00:16:40.644 --> 00:16:45.292
He walks up to the front door of the house.

00:16:45.352 --> 00:16:53.303
He is carrying his notebook, and he has a list of questions to ask the playwright.

00:16:53.363 --> 00:16:58.627
But he is a little afraid of the famous man.

00:16:58.687 --> 00:17:03.936
Zoe follows Mike to Todd Marin's house.

00:17:03.996 --> 00:17:10.718
She is careful and she follows Mike very quietly.

00:17:10.778 --> 00:17:16.329
Zoe is acting the part of Kate Lawson again.

00:17:16.389 --> 00:17:25.434
She has a black wig over her hair and she is wearing glasses.

00:17:25.494 --> 00:17:38.952
She hides behind one of the bushes in front of Todd Marin's house and watches Mike go to the front door.

00:17:39.012 --> 00:17:44.564
It is a big dark house.

00:17:44.624 --> 00:17:51.256
This is funny, she thinks smiling.

00:17:51.316 --> 00:18:01.053
When Todd Marin opens the door of his house, Mike begins to talk quickly.

00:18:01.113 --> 00:18:06.358
Hello, Mr. Marin, he says.

00:18:06.418 --> 00:18:09.542
I'm Mike Morrison.

00:18:09.602 --> 00:18:16.983
I'm a student at Newport College, and I want to write plays.

00:18:17.043 --> 00:18:21.652
Do you, Todd Marin says?

00:18:21.712 --> 00:18:30.302
And I write reviews in the Newport Weekly News, Mike tells him.

00:18:30.363 --> 00:18:36.250
What do you want from me, Todd Marin asks?

00:18:36.310 --> 00:18:42.266
Can I ask you some questions, Mike says?

00:18:42.326 --> 00:18:50.573
Why, Marin asks, is it for the Newport Weekly News?

00:18:50.633 --> 00:18:54.216
That's a difficult question.

00:18:54.276 --> 00:18:58.390
What do I do now, Mike thinks?

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:05.726
Do I tell him a lie or do I tell him the truth?

00:19:05.786 --> 00:19:16.684
Then, after a second or two, he says, it's for Yes Magazine.

00:19:16.744 --> 00:19:32.760
Listen, I know it's a stupid magazine, but come into the house, Todd Marin says suddenly.

00:19:32.820 --> 00:19:53.893
Chapter 5: Zoe Waits. Zoe is watching Mike and Todd Marin from behind a bush.

00:19:53.953 --> 00:20:00.546
She can see them, but she cannot hear them speaking.

00:20:00.606 --> 00:20:05.856
She sees Todd Marin open the door.

00:20:05.916 --> 00:20:11.518
And she sees Mike follow him into the house.

00:20:11.578 --> 00:20:14.750
Zoe smiles.

00:20:14.810 --> 00:20:16.452
Right.

00:20:16.512 --> 00:20:20.424
He's in the house, she thinks.

00:20:20.484 --> 00:20:28.301
Now, let's wait for Todd Marin to throw him out.

00:20:28.361 --> 00:20:33.940
Todd Marin takes Mike to his study.

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:41.539
There are hundreds of books in the room and a big desk.

00:20:41.600 --> 00:20:47.352
Todd goes and sits behind the desk.

00:20:47.412 --> 00:20:54.460
Thank you for telling me the truth," he says to Mike.

00:20:54.520 --> 00:20:59.742
I can see you're an honest young man.

00:20:59.802 --> 00:21:07.085
You can ask your questions, but not for Yes Magazine.

00:21:07.145 --> 00:21:09.106
You're right.

00:21:09.166 --> 00:21:12.697
It is a stupid magazine.

00:21:12.757 --> 00:21:16.431
I hate gossip magazines.

00:21:16.491 --> 00:21:20.216
Why do people write for them?

00:21:20.276 --> 00:21:27.320
Because they pay a lot of money, I believe, Mike says.

00:21:27.380 --> 00:21:29.962
Todd Marin laughs.

00:21:30.022 --> 00:21:35.304
Yes, you're right again, he says.

00:21:35.364 --> 00:21:40.668
But you can write about me for the Newport Weekly News.

00:21:40.728 --> 00:21:42.842
Is that okay?

00:21:42.902 --> 00:21:51.387
Yes, that's okay," Mike says, and he smiles at Todd Marin happily.

00:21:51.447 --> 00:21:57.049
I like to help young writers with ideas when I can.

00:21:57.109 --> 00:21:59.230
Todd says kindly.

00:21:59.290 --> 00:22:01.340
Sit down.

00:22:01.400 --> 00:22:09.339
Mike sits down, puts his notebook on Todd's desk and opens it.

00:22:09.399 --> 00:22:16.368
I read your reviews in the newspaper sometimes, Todd says.

00:22:16.428 --> 00:22:19.420
They're very good.

00:22:19.480 --> 00:22:25.482
Well, I think they're okay, Mike says.

00:22:25.542 --> 00:22:31.464
But I want to write for the theatre, TV and movies.

00:22:31.524 --> 00:22:34.596
I'm writing a play now.

00:22:34.656 --> 00:22:36.527
Are you?

00:22:36.587 --> 00:22:40.162
Tell me about it, Todd says.

00:22:40.222 --> 00:22:42.077
Can I?

00:22:42.138 --> 00:22:48.970
Mike asks, well, it's about a boy and a girl.

00:22:49.030 --> 00:22:51.722
A boy and a girl?

00:22:51.782 --> 00:22:53.462
That's right.

00:22:53.522 --> 00:23:04.688
They, Todd Marin, sits back in his chair to listen, and Mike tells him the plot of his play.

00:23:04.748 --> 00:23:08.028
Mike is very nervous.

00:23:08.088 --> 00:23:12.018
But Todd Marin does not speak.

00:23:12.078 --> 00:23:19.582
He smiles at Mike, and he listens to him very carefully.

00:23:19.642 --> 00:23:24.183
When at last Mike stops speaking.

00:23:24.243 --> 00:23:27.604
Todd says, thank you.

00:23:27.664 --> 00:23:30.645
That's very interesting.

00:23:30.705 --> 00:23:35.822
It's a good story, and it's funny too.

00:23:35.882 --> 00:23:42.110
But there are one or two things you can do to make it better.

00:23:42.171 --> 00:23:50.476
To begin with, Zoe stays behind the bush and waits.

00:23:50.537 --> 00:23:55.150
An hour goes by and nothing happens.

00:23:55.210 --> 00:23:58.644
She is getting impatient.

00:23:58.704 --> 00:24:02.300
What are they doing in there?

00:24:02.360 --> 00:24:04.163
She thinks.

00:24:04.223 --> 00:24:10.821
Todd Marin never gives interviews to gossip magazines.

00:24:10.881 --> 00:24:15.280
So what are they talking about?

00:24:15.340 --> 00:24:24.242
She remembers Mike Morrison's review of Romeo and Juliet in the newspaper.

00:24:24.302 --> 00:24:37.384
She remembers his words about her acting, and she wants to see his face when Todd Marin throws him out of the house.

00:24:37.444 --> 00:24:41.027
How long must I wait?

00:24:41.087 --> 00:24:48.167
She thinks impatiently.

00:24:48.227 --> 00:25:13.080
Chapter 6: Telling the Truth. After an hour and a half, Mike Morrison leaves Todd Marin's study and comes out of the house.

00:25:13.140 --> 00:25:21.450
He and the playwright are smiling and Mike is saying, thank you.

00:25:21.510 --> 00:25:29.774
They talk for two or three minutes and Zoe watches them from behind the bush.

00:25:29.834 --> 00:25:33.084
She is amazed.

00:25:33.144 --> 00:25:35.685
What's happening?

00:25:35.745 --> 00:25:37.486
She thinks.

00:25:37.546 --> 00:25:41.708
Why are they so friendly?

00:25:41.768 --> 00:25:47.699
After a minute or two more, they shake hands.

00:25:47.759 --> 00:25:57.100
Then Todd Marin goes back into the house and Mike Morrison walks away.

00:25:57.160 --> 00:26:02.842
Mike sees Kate Lawson waiting for him.

00:26:02.902 --> 00:26:05.632
Oh, hello.

00:26:05.692 --> 00:26:08.172
He says nervously.

00:26:08.232 --> 00:26:12.436
He is surprised to see her so soon.

00:26:12.496 --> 00:26:16.021
Are you waiting for me?

00:26:16.082 --> 00:26:20.814
Yes, she says impatiently.

00:26:20.874 --> 00:26:24.756
I'm waiting for your interview.

00:26:24.816 --> 00:26:31.039
Look, I can't lie to you, he replies.

00:26:31.099 --> 00:26:35.752
There's no interview or Yes Magazine.

00:26:35.812 --> 00:26:43.703
Mr. Marin always refuses to talk to reporters from gossip magazines.

00:26:43.764 --> 00:26:48.443
But what? Kate begins.

00:26:48.504 --> 00:26:53.756
What can two people talk about for an hour and a half?

00:26:53.816 --> 00:27:02.660
Mike says, laughing, about writing, about characters, and about plot.

00:27:02.721 --> 00:27:08.032
Nothing for Yes Magazine, I'm afraid.

00:27:08.092 --> 00:27:21.682
Oh, I have my list of questions and Mr. Marin's answers, but my interview is for the Newport Weekly News.

00:27:21.742 --> 00:27:27.316
And I know a lot more about writing plays now.

00:27:27.376 --> 00:27:31.592
He's very interested in my play.

00:27:31.652 --> 00:27:36.679
Your play, Kate says furiously.

00:27:36.699 --> 00:27:44.094
Yes, I'm writing a play for TV, Mike says.

00:27:44.154 --> 00:27:47.746
And Mr. Marin wants to read it.

00:27:47.807 --> 00:27:53.190
He can help me with the characters and the plot.

00:27:53.250 --> 00:27:58.014
Well, that's nice, she says.

00:27:58.074 --> 00:28:04.138
Say hello to Mike Morrison, the famous playwright.

00:28:04.198 --> 00:28:12.332
He writes stupid reviews for the Newport Weekly News, but his plays are okay.

00:28:12.392 --> 00:28:16.423
You're angry, Mike says.

00:28:16.484 --> 00:28:22.006
Listen, I'm sorry about the interview for Yes.

00:28:22.066 --> 00:28:25.206
Kate laughs.

00:28:25.226 --> 00:28:28.958
No, it's okay, she says.

00:28:29.019 --> 00:28:31.870
I'm not angry.

00:28:31.931 --> 00:28:37.814
And then she does something very strange.

00:28:37.875 --> 00:28:41.802
She takes off her wig.

00:28:41.862 --> 00:28:45.030
She's wearing a wig.

00:28:45.090 --> 00:28:47.953
Mike thinks, 'I'm mad.'.

00:28:48.013 --> 00:28:55.090
Next, she takes off her glasses and she smiles at Mike.

00:28:55.150 --> 00:28:59.094
And now he knows her.

00:28:59.154 --> 00:29:02.266
He begins to laugh.

00:29:02.326 --> 00:29:06.911
You're not Kate Lawson, he says.

00:29:06.971 --> 00:29:12.564
You're That's right," Zoe says.

00:29:12.624 --> 00:29:19.005
I'm a 17-year-old girl in an older woman's costume.

00:29:19.065 --> 00:29:26.966
Mr. Mike Morrison, review writer for the Newport Weekly News.

00:29:27.026 --> 00:29:32.028
Mike's face is very red now.

00:29:32.088 --> 00:29:35.080
He feels embarrassed.

00:29:35.140 --> 00:29:37.844
What a trick!

00:29:37.904 --> 00:29:45.758
So there is no Kate Lawson editor of Yes Magazine, he says.

00:29:45.818 --> 00:29:50.812
No, there isn't, Zoe says laughing.

00:29:50.872 --> 00:29:53.654
What do you think now?

00:29:53.714 --> 00:29:56.696
Does this prove something?

00:29:56.756 --> 00:30:00.134
Am I a good actress?

00:30:00.194 --> 00:30:04.794
Yes, you are a good actress."

00:30:04.854 --> 00:30:07.766
Mike says, laughing with her.

00:30:07.826 --> 00:30:13.701
And I'm going to put that in the Newport Weekly News.

00:30:13.761 --> 00:30:15.542
Are you?

00:30:15.602 --> 00:30:17.344
Zoe says.

00:30:17.404 --> 00:30:25.650
Yes, and thanks for making me go and see Todd Marin, Mike tells her.

00:30:25.711 --> 00:30:29.379
He doesn't feel embarrassed anymore.

00:30:29.439 --> 00:30:34.852
Now I can get help with my play," he says.

00:30:34.913 --> 00:30:41.964
Come on, let's get a cup of coffee and I'm paying.

00:30:42.024 --> 00:30:52.091
Well, I can't refuse a free coffee, Zoe says, and she laughs.

00:30:52.151 --> 00:30:55.146
End of side two.